    "h24_crosscheck": "DISCREPANCY STATED HONESTLY, because it is ~1pp and would otherwise be silently glossed. DexScreener prints h24 = -2.86% on the deepest pair and -3.74% / -3.79% / -4.03% / -4.42% on the other four Base pairs; the five disagree with EACH OTHER by 1.56pp, which alone proves these are sampled rolling figures, not block-pinned ones. Block-pinned on-chain value: -3.848%. The gap is methodology, not an arithmetic error: DexScreener samples last-trade prices at two wall-clock instants, whereas this run compares reserves at exactly ts(head)-86400 and converts through one specified VIRTUAL/USDC pool. VIRTUAL's own h24 also differs by source (-2.46% on the deepest VIRTUAL/WETH pair vs -2.671% measured on-chain via VIRTUAL/USDC), and that 0.21pp propagates straight into the DEUS figure. GATE IMPACT: none - both readings sit 100x+ outside the 20% sharp-move gate, and neither ATH ($0.06876, +297%) nor any target (nearest is $0.012 at -30.6%) is close to being touched. RULE: for any precise distance-to-gate number, use the on-chain mark, never the API.",
    "h24_note": "h24 -3.848% over the EXACT 86400s window (blk 53014374 ts 1792818095 -> head 53057574 ts 1792904495; asserted ts(head)-ts(pin) == 86400). Decomposed against a DIRECT VIRTUAL/USDC mark: VIRTUAL/DEUS ratio 0.0280085435 -> 0.0276698249 = -1.209%; DEUS IN the pool +115,060.13 (+0.610%); VIRTUAL IN the pool -3,203.12 (-0.607%); VIRTUAL/USD 0.643980 -> 0.626781 = -2.671%. USD mark 0.01803695 -> 0.01734292 = -3.848%. METHOD: the ratio leg and the DEUS-in-pool leg are the SAME event counted twice (constant product: DEUS in / VIRTUAL out), the -2.671% quote leg is independent, and the two compound to -3.848%. Do NOT add the three legs. NO supply withdrawal in either direction."
