    "read": "ONE large seller (50,167) against 37 small buyers (median 774 DEUS, total 34,753). Net result is +15,414 DEUS INTO the pool, i.e. the seller out-supplied the buyers by 1.4x and the mark still rose +0.355% in VIRTUAL terms. That combination is important: the ratio rose, so the buyers were paying up even while being out-supplied - but the pool is absorbing DEUS, which is the direction that eventually pressures price. Watch whether the 37-buyer cohort is the same handful of addresses recycling (that would be wash/arb) or genuinely distinct payers. The first hour only had 1 seller, so this is not yet a cascade."
  },
