    "funding": "The executor received its 101,983.48 over THREE inbound transfers, all from 1inch-family routers: 65,552.78 from 0x111111125421ca6dc452d289314280a0f8842a65 at blk 52985282, 22,081.55 from 0x7d6839415693801e94cdc4a7d732c9a3fdbbd1d7 at blk 53022841, 14,349.15 from 0x1111111254... at blk 53026431. ZERO transfers directly from CLAIM vault or any known distributor — so on the evidence available this is NOT a claim-and-dump. It is an aggregator route consuming a pre-existing balance. Do not label it vesting without the upstream hop.",
    "why_it_matters": "This is the first print on record of a 6-figure DEUS sell executing through an aggregator bundle rather than a naked pool sell. It changes the sell-side model: one operator can now clear 100k across five venues in a single block, so the 'thin book / one clip per block' assumption is dead. Impact was still only -0.70% because 5 pools shared it — the deepest pool only took 66k net."
